Let's find the amount of money Callan spends on each ingredient. Then we can add all these up to find the total sum.

For example, flour costs $0.80$ dollars per kilogram and Callan uses $x$ kilograms of it, so Callan spends $0.8x$ dollars on flour:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\left(0.80\,\dfrac{\text{dollars}}{\text{kilogram}}\right)\left(x\,\text{kilograms}\right)
\\\\
&=0.8x\,\dfrac{\text{dollars}}{\cancel{\text{kilogram}}}\cdot\,\cancel{\text{kilograms}}
\\\\
&=0.8x\,\text{dollars}
\end{align}$
